{"tool_name":"superdsm","contents":["galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","neubias","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"superdsm","home":"https://github.com/BMCV/SuperDSM","license":"MIT","summary":"SuperDSM is a globally optimal segmentation method based on superadditivity and deformable shape models for cell nuclei in fluorescence microscopy images and beyond.","addition_date":"2023-11-02T14:34:00.260124Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:31:33.938814Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:superdsm","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"leonid.kostrykin@bioquant.uni-heidelberg.de","name":"Leonid Kostrykin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1323-3762","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://kostrykin.com"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation","Command-line options","Installation instructions","Quick start guide","User manual"],"url":"https://superdsm.readthedocs.io"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"cmd":"python -m 'superdsm.batch' --help","operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"SuperDSM","owner":"kostrykin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1109/tpami.2022.3185583","metadata":{"abstract":"Cell nuclei segmentation is challenging due to shape variation and closely clustered or partially overlapping objects. Most previous methods are not globally optimal, limited to elliptical models, or are computationally expensive. In this work, we introduce a globally optimal approach based on deformable shape models and global energy minimization for cell nuclei segmentation and cluster splitting. We propose an implicit parameterization of deformable shape models and show that it leads to a convex energy. Convex energy minimization yields the global solution independently of the initialization, is fast, and robust. To jointly perform cell nuclei segmentation and cluster splitting, we developed a novel iterative global energy minimization method, which leverages the inherent property of superadditivity of the convex energy. This property exploits the lower bound of the energy of the union of the models and improves the computational efficiency. Our method provably determines a solution close to global optimality. In addition, we derive a closed-form solution of the proposed global minimization based on the superadditivity property for non-clustered cell nuclei. We evaluated our method using fluorescence microscopy images of five different cell types comprising various challenges, and performed a quantitative comparison with previous methods. Our method achieved state-of-the-art or improved performance.","authors":[{"name":"Kostrykin L."},{"name":"Rohr K."}],"citationCount":2,"date":"2023-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","title":"Superadditivity and Convex Optimization for Globally Optimal Cell Segmentation Using Deformable Shape Models"},"pmid":"35737620","type":["Primary"]}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SuperDSM","home":"https://bio.tools/superdsm","license":"MIT","summary":"SuperDSM is a globally optimal segmentation method based on superadditivity and deformable shape models for cell nuclei in fluorescence microscopy images and beyond.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@","first_commit":"2023-06-20","conda_name":"superdsm","conda_version":"0.4.0","summary":"Globally optimal segmentation method based on superadditivity and deformable shape models for cell nuclei in fluorescence microscopy images","edam_operations":["Image analysis"],"edam_topics":[],"toolshed_categories":["Imaging"],"toolshed_id":"superdsm","users_5_years":5,"users_all_time":5,"usage_5_years":26,"usage_all_time":26,"bio_tools_summary":"SuperDSM is a globally optimal segmentation method based on superadditivity and deformable shape models for cell nuclei i